<item>
            <title>[LU-20826] sanity-sec test_31: MDC import should have failnid (review-ldiskfs-arm)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20826</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-sec test_31 failed on review-ldiskfs-arm (el8.10 x86_64 servers, Rocky 9.8 aarch64 clients):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;MDC import should have failnid 10.240.22.34@tcp999
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After test_31, 32 more subtests failed (nodemap, set_param, umount). This looks like the cluster was left in a bad state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Session: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/6f481f5d-c419-4c1b-8a1e-5c2458b9fa44&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/6f481f5d-c419-4c1b-8a1e-5c2458b9fa44&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Change: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/68157&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/68157&lt;/a&gt; (patch set 26), userspace llapi only.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The review-ldiskfs-arm sessions on the changes above it in the same series (68158, 68159, 68160, 68163), which include its code, passed 6/6.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_31 history on lustre-reviews, last 400 sessions: 310 pass, 2 fail. Both failures are on this series, with different errors: this one, and &apos;writeconf failed&apos; on 68094 patch set 23.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
